  "rendered_prompt": "<|system|>You are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|end|><|user|>Paragraph:\n\"\"\"\nArtificial intelligence tools like chatbots are becoming common in schools, and teachers are not sure how to handle them. Some teachers worry that students will use AI to write their essays and never learn how to think for themselves. Others believe AI can be a useful tutor that explains hard ideas in a simple way. In my experience, AI is most helpful when I use it to check my understanding, not to do the work for me. Schools should teach students how to use these tools honestly instead of banning them completely.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer selected this text:\n\"\"\"\nOthers believe AI can be a useful tutor that explains hard ideas in a simple way.\n\"\"\"\n\nGive 5 different rewrites of the selected text that use new wording but keep about the same length. Keep the meaning, facts, names, numbers and quotations. Each rewrite must read naturally in place of the original. Put the best options first.<|end|><|assistant|>",
